next: **CRAN SUBMISSION ON HOLD — user called a hold 2026-08-17 00:52 MDT; do NOT submit or merge dev->main without explicit go-ahead.** v1.7.0 is published on GitHub as a PRE-RELEASE only (tag `v1.7.0` on `dev`); `main` deliberately remains at 1.6.1, which is what CRAN serves. Users can get the fix via `remotes::install_github("Data-Wise/RMediation", ref = "dev")`. v1.7.0 fixes issue #27: `pprodnormal3()` returned silently wrong probabilities on ill-conditioned covariance (24% error at rho=0.999, 92% relative in the lower tail, at every q). Default integrator is now `method="gauss"`; `"hcubature"` retained for cross-checking. **The open decision, if the hold is reconsidered: making "gauss" the default changes returned values for every user — that is the one choice that becomes irreversible once on CRAN.** Gates all green: 424 tests pass (0 fail/warn/skip; 345 -> 424 after PR #30's coverage work), `R CMD check --as-cran` 0 errors/0 warnings (1 local-only NOTE, HTML-Tidy version, not CRAN-relevant), test coverage 71.70% (up from 55.45%), r-hub 3/3 pass (linux/windows/macos-arm64, 2026-08-17), win-builder 3/3 Status: OK — R-devel (r90413), R-release (4.6.1), R-oldrelease (4.5.3), all received 2026-08-17 and confirmed in Gmail 2026-08-21. `cran-comments.md` is complete for 1.7.0: r-hub and all three win-builder results filled in, nothing left PENDING; a 2026-08-22 addendum documents the post-dispatch `mvtnorm` Suggests addition and coverage work (test-only, not independently re-dispatched to r-hub/win-builder). **Every technical gate is green and the 2026-08-21 cadence window has opened — the only thing outstanding is the hold itself and the `method="gauss"` default decision.** Issues #26 and #27 stay open on GitHub until dev->main. Live pkgdown site is at 1.7.0 (deployed from the tag before that trigger was removed) while CRAN is 1.6.1 — deliberate, see SPEC-29.

