## Session 2026-08-16 (issue #27 prod3 integrator + #26 Shiny links, v1.7.0)
- Issue #26 (docs, on `dev`, commit a5b0178): README "Try It Online" section +
  pkgdown `home:` link to https://data-wise.github.io/mediation-apps/ (both 200).
- Issue #27 (code, `feature/prod3-illconditioned`, PR #28): reproduced the bug
  against installed 1.6.1 (24.29% error at rho=0.999, matching the report to 4dp),
  then validated the proposed remedy before implementing it — which changed it:
  - Axis partitioning ALONE is insufficient (1.96e-01 -> 5.87e-02, still 7.3% off).
    Gauss-Legendre is the fix; partitioning is its prerequisite. Unpartitioned
    Gauss returns 2.11 — not a probability.
  - Bug is wider than reported: every q, worst 92% relative at q=-2. confint()/
    ci()/dist_quantile() inherit it because they invert this CDF.
  - References pinned to GL self-consistency (1e-14 across n=512/1024/2048), not
    Monte Carlo — MC at 1e7 has 3SE=3.7e-04, too noisy, and two seeds disagreed
    by more than the errors being measured.
  - Truncation bound derived from a tail-mass argument, not tuned: at bound=4
    successive rules agree to 1.7e-14 while being 3.2e-05 wrong — the same
    failure signature as the bug being fixed.
  - Second silent legacy failure found: hcubature returns exactly 0 at
    standardized means beyond ~8 (true value ~0.46). Unrelated to conditioning.
- Root cause of why it shipped: test-product-normal3.R:91 was named "handles
  near-singular covariance", ran rho=0.99, and asserted only expect_no_error()
  plus 0<=p<=1. That case was already wrong by 1.8e-03.
- Also closed issue #17 (machine `status:` header — already present).
- Released v1.7.0 on GitHub (tag on `dev`, pre-release) so the fix ships ahead of
  the CRAN cadence window; `main` deliberately left at 1.6.1 = the CRAN version.
- Two `/code-review` rounds after the fix landed:
  - Round 1 flagged the signed-cell partition at `|m| > bound` as broken. Verified
    against Monte Carlo instead of accepted: it is correct by construction (the
    cells telescope to the intended box), and the suggested clamp would have
    introduced a real bug. Comment + regression test added so it is not
    "fixed" later. Verifying it turned up the large-mean hcubature collapse.
  - Round 2 (PR #29) found a genuine defect of mine: `@param diagnostics`
    promised `"error"` is NA for hcubature while the code always passed that
    integrator's own estimate through. Resolved by keeping the value and
    documenting it as untrustworthy + not comparable across methods.
  - Also fixed 8 British spellings (6 mine) and scoped the nodes/NA claim.
- `R CMD check --as-cran` on dev initially raised 2 NOTEs the worktree never saw
  (SPEC-*.md at top level, `.token-optimizer` dir). Both .Rbuildignore'd in
  982cecf — would have hit at CRAN submission.
- Docs: SPEC-26, SPEC-27 (design + evidence), SPEC-28 (review triage) on dev.


